Imports:
  - Types:
      - FilterList
      - MangasPage
      - Page
      - SChapter
      - SManga
      - SMangaUpdate
    From: source-api/src/main/kotlin/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/source/model

Usages:
  default_method_bridging: |
    Source's primary suspend methods (getPopularManga, getLatestUpdates, getSearchManga,
    getMangaUpdate, getPageList) each have a default implementation. CatalogueSource
    overrides them to bridge to the older RxJava fetch* methods for sources that have not
    migrated; a source that implements the suspend methods directly does not need to touch the
    fetch* methods at all, and vice versa.

Annotations: |
  This is the extension contract every manga/comic source implements: the in-process
  LocalSource (not documented in this forest), or an out-of-process extension APK loaded by
  Mihon's external extension-loading mechanism (not part of this repository). Everything the
  host app can ask a source to do is declared here; nothing about how a source fetches or parses
  data is.

  Use SManga/SChapter/`MangasPage`/`Page`/`FilterList`/`SMangaUpdate` from Imports throughout.
  Use `default_method_bridging` for the relationship between Source and CatalogueSource.

---

"Source()":
  location: Source.kt
  annotations: |
    The minimal contract any source (network-backed or local) must satisfy to supply manga and
    chapters to the app.

    Use `default_method_bridging`.
  properties:
    "id -> Long": |
      Unique source id.
    "name -> String": |
      Source display name.
    "lang -> String": |
      Source language code, empty string if not applicable (e.g. an aggregator).
    "supportsLatest -> Boolean": |
      Whether getLatestUpdates returns meaningful results for this source.
  methods:
    "getFilterList() -> filters:FilterList": |
      The filters this source supports for getSearchManga, in the order they should be
      presented to the user. Default: no filters.
    "getPopularManga(page: Int) -> mangas:MangasPage": |
      One page of the source's "popular" manga listing.
    "getLatestUpdates(page: Int) -> mangas:MangasPage": |
      One page of the source's "latest updates" listing.
    "getSearchManga(page: Int, query: String, filters: FilterList) -> mangas:MangasPage": |
      One page of search results for `query`, refined by `filters` (previously obtained from
      getFilterList() and mutated by the user).
    "getMangaUpdate(manga: SManga, chapters: List<SChapter>, fetchDetails: Boolean, fetchChapters: Boolean) -> update:SMangaUpdate": |
      Refresh one manga's metadata and/or chapter list.

      fetchDetails: when false, the returned SMangaUpdate.manga may be `manga` unchanged
      fetchChapters: when false, the returned SMangaUpdate.chapters may be `chapters`
      unchanged

      Requirements:
      - Only return metadata the source can vouch for; the host app applies whatever is
        returned regardless of the flags
    "getPageList(chapter: SChapter) -> pages:List<Page>": |
      The ordered list of page images for `chapter`. Page.index need not be pre-sorted; order
      of the returned list is what is used.

"Source::ConfigurableSource()":
  location: ConfigurableSource.kt
  annotations: |
    Mutation of Source for sources that expose user-configurable settings in the app's
    settings UI.
  methods:
    "getSourcePreferences() -> preferences:SharedPreferences": |
      The `SharedPreferences` instance scoped to this source (namespaced by id).
    "setupPreferenceScreen(screen: PreferenceScreen)": |
      Populate `screen` with this source's configurable preference entries.

"Source::CatalogueSource()":
  location: CatalogueSource.kt
  annotations: |
    Mutation of Source for sources that additionally declare a fixed lang (rather than the
    default empty string) and support the filtered-search flow. This is the contract concrete
    manga/comic sources implement in practice.

    Use `default_method_bridging`.
  properties:
    "lang -> String": |
      ISO 639-1 language code this source instance serves; unlike Source.lang, not optional.

"UnmeteredSource()":
  location: UnmeteredSource.kt
  annotations: |
    Marker interface, with no members, applied to a Source (typically a self-hosted one) to
    signal that request-rate/traffic considerations the host app applies to other sources do not
    apply to it.

"SourceFactory()":
  location: SourceFactory.kt
  annotations: |
    A source may implement this instead of Source directly when a single extension needs to
    expose more than one logical source (e.g. one source per language variant).
  methods:
    "createSources() -> sources:List<Source>": |
      Build every Source instance this factory provides.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  The behavioral half of the source-api extension contract. Source/CatalogueSource are
  implemented by exactly one in-repo type, LocalSource (not documented in this forest), and by
  an unbounded number of out-of-process extension APKs loaded through a mechanism outside this
  repository; the contract itself is the load-bearing artifact regardless of where an
  implementation lives.
